# Testing and verify flows

## Two layers

| Layer | Location | Needs live stack? | Owns |
|-------|----------|-------------------|------|
| **Unit** | `tests/unit/` | No | Pure functions, auth helpers, BFF shaping, role checks, i18n keys |
| **Live verify** | `tests/verify/` | Yes | Full BFF + UI journeys, cookie session, upstream integration |

**SSOT for ownership:** `tests/README.md` feature map — must match `as-built/implementation-status.md` verification rows.

## Unit tests (Vitest)

- Home: **`tests/unit/`** only
- Mock upstream `fetch`; do not start Next.js server for business-logic tests
- Prefer testing `lib/*` helpers, error mappers, pagination, role gates

## Live verify

- Playwright, scripted HTTP against `next dev`, or documented manual smoke with reproducible steps
- May call real upstream when stack is up — document env in `tests/README.md`
- One verify path per feature; trim or add scripts when feature map changes

## No-overlap policy

- **Do not** duplicate a full HTTP journey in Vitest if live verify already covers it
- **Do** unit-test branching logic, parsers, and edge cases extracted from route handlers
- Verify module headers should cite which unit tests own shared logic

## Closure (qualitative)

No numeric quotas on test count. Closure = feature map complete, as-built agrees, every in-scope capability has unit and/or live verify proof.

## CI

```bash
npm run lint && npm run types && npm run format:check && npm run test && npm run build
```

Live verify is optional in CI when documented as manual/board **Verify command**; prefer scripted verify when feasible.
